    "title": "WVU Men's Soccer falls in double OT in Sun Belt semis | West Virginia University Sports | wvnews.com",
    "text": "MORGANTOWN, W.Va. -- The No. 17/No. 2-seed West Virginia University men’s soccer team fell in the Sun Belt semifinals by a 3-2 score in double overtime to No. 12/No. 3-seed Marshall on Wednesday evening at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium. The Mountaineers fall to 12-4-3 while the Thundering Herd improve to 11-2-5.\nWest Virginia had to rally twice in the match after falling behind on two occasions, getting goals from sophomore Isaac Scheer and senior Marcus Caldeira in the second half. Junior Constantinos Christou collected an assist for WVU.",
